        "text": "People naturally tend to view younger generations as inferior in intelligence compared to their own.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "Intelligence should be measured by exposure to modern educational content, not just traditional knowledge.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "Cultural and technological changes necessitate new forms of knowledge acquisition.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "Older generations lack familiarity with current educational content due to generational differences.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "Perceived decline in youth intelligence reflects bias rather than actual cognitive deterioration.",
