  {
    "episode_id": 85641,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/5/85641.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 33,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, I would totally agree with that. Every generation always laments that the next generation following them, has it better? They're so spoiled. They just don't try as hard. They're lazy. They're too liberal. This is a common refrain, right? We've always heard this. The world never moves toward the more conservative side hardly ever. It always becomes more liberal, if you will. And I'm not saying that in a good or bad way. I'm just making the observation. And it's not necessarily a political way either, but just liberal ideology about various things. And things in a lot of ways keep getting better. I mean, they're not all better, but it's interesting. Anything you want to share more about health, or I'd love to hear about scientific betting too. I know that's a different subject, but just on any of your other work as well before",
